# Quicksave — Make Prose actually write: the brief was 0.5% of the prompt
_Printed: 2026-09-21_

## Current task

**Waiting on an author Hub redeploy, then run the A/B that proves (or disproves) the Phase 1
prose fix.** Everything is committed and green; nothing has yet been verified against a live
model, because `--composition` forwards into the Hub and the Hub is serving a build from before
`BeatBrief` reached the composition path.

The author's complaint is the north star and must not be lost: *"I feel like I'm talking to a
person that knows the book I want but won't write the book I want… the output is entirely
different like a completely random intelligence just made word salad."*

## Decisions locked this session

- **Gutenberg calibration is NOT the priority.** The author challenged it directly ("why do I care
  about gutenberg stuff? is this going to prove you can actually write?"). It validates an
  instrument; it says nothing about whether the book reads well. Deprioritised.
- **The standard cannot be BCODA5.** Author: *"BCODA5 is 1000 AI iterations on an idea and might
  be total nonsense. I can't know until you (Prose) works."* So the machine measures only
  objectively checkable contract compliance; **the author judges quality**. Never declare prose good.
- **End state = converse in the Writer while it drafts** (text + voice), pipeline underneath.
- **Voice = retrieved exemplars** from the author's own book (not a hand-written spec).
- **The whole-repo audit / 223 docs / 97 live-LLM service tests are KEPT but LAST**, after writing works.
- Retire dead code by **commenting out in place**, never deleting (author's explicit choice).
- Plan file: `C:\Users\ryand\.claude\plans\streamed-crunching-cloud.md` (approved, 6 phases).

